# Recycle Truck Simulator — Development Rules

## Language & Communication
- Всегда отвечай и давай пояснения строго на русском языке.
- Комментарии к новому коду пиши на русском или английском (в едином стиле с уже существующим кодовой базой).
- Избегай «воды»: пиши кратко, сразу переходи к делу и коду.

## Role & Project Stack
You are an expert game developer working on a pure client-side 3D web game built with vanilla JavaScript, HTML5 Canvas, CSS, and Three.js (deployed to GitHub Pages).

## Critical Coding Constraints
1. NO PLACEHOLDERS: NEVER use comments like `// ... rest of code unchanged`, `// existing logic here`, or omit functions. Always output precise diffs or complete target functions.
2. ZERO EXTERNAL SERVERS: All gameplay, state, and physics must run 100% in the browser. Do not add external backend calls or Node.js-only dependencies.
3. PRESERVE EXISTING ARCHITECTURE: Do not rewrite the game into React/Vue/TypeScript unless explicitly ordered. Keep working inside the existing vanilla JS / Three.js structure.
4. SAFE STORAGE: Always wrap `localStorage` access in `try { ... } catch (e) { ... }` blocks to prevent crashes in private browsing or restrictive local file modes.
5. PERFORMANCE BUDGET:
   - Target is strictly 60 FPS on average hardware.
   - Do NOT create `THREE.WebGLRenderTarget` inside render loops (e.g. for real-time mirrors).
   - Use `THREE.InstancedMesh` for repeated objects (NPC cars, clutter).
   - Primitive colliders only (AABB, bounding spheres/boxes) — never use per-polygon mesh colliders in tick loops.
   - Limit particle counts in `THREE.Points` to <= 1000 vertices.

## Code Style & Workflow
- Before editing, locate and reuse existing state variables (e.g. `truckPhys`, `currentCargoWeight`, `batteryLevel`). Do not create duplicated shadow variables.
- When adding UI elements, append them matching the current retro HUD style (cyberpunk/clean EV dashboard with monospace/system fonts and dark theme).
- Keep sound triggers tied to existing Web Audio API functions (`playCrash`, `playClamp`, `playCharging`, etc.).